        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-16T15:19:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "At one point, Peng or Quyen had had a CL to add size to BindBufferInfo directly, since the size of the sub allocation can help bind groups for DrawPasses too. They avoided it by just using the max allowable bind size as a pessimistic limit if the buffer itself was larger.\n\nI\u0027d had concerns about making BindBufferInfo larger, but being able to identify non-overlapping views seems like a critical use case. In practice, we probably don\u0027t care about the full `size_t` range and could change size and offset to both be uint32_t\u0027s and fit all of this data into the one struct.\n\nThis may necessitate some larger changes in DrawWriter in order to shrink its BindBufferInfos to the written range, but I think that can happen naturally when it returns data to the buffer manager.\n\nWDYT? I\u0027m open to landing this and migrating to one struct later if that becomes a larger change. I don\u0027t want to block the compute work too much.",
      "revId": "daa850c41f653c9e96ab9476bd999da913ce4260",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6d63f94f_c62442c8",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-16T19:39:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually this is the route I wanted to take initially but felt less inclined to do so because I remember the discussion on that CL you\u0027re referring to 😊\n\nI think adding this to BindBufferInfo is a good idea in general and it will simplify code that carries a side-car size field only because BindBufferInfo doesn\u0027t (this CL and `ClearBufferInfo` are two examples). I\u0027m not entirely sure if it\u0027s a good idea to move to `uint32_t`, then again I don\u0027t quite foresee us allocating buffers that are \u003e4GB in size.\n\n\u003e WDYT? I\u0027m open to landing this and migrating to one struct later if that becomes a larger change. I don\u0027t want to block the compute work too much.\n\nI prefer to land this now as is, not because I want to avoid the work, but because it will require some changes to BufferManager code to make sure that it returns the correct size and I may want to couple that with some unit tests. I\u0027m going to file a bug for the task and I\u0027m happy to take it on as a follow-up.",
      "parentUuid": "20e15bef_bb5caefc",
      "revId": "daa850c41f653c9e96ab9476bd999da913ce4260",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e299a05d_17fb61a6",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-16T19:44:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think \u003c4GB is pretty safe for the buffer binding, given the binding size restrictions on the GPU backends. And we already have plenty of other limits that are even lower (i.e. 65k high-level draws). For value types that get passed around a lot I definitely like to keep them as small as possible.",
      "parentUuid": "6d63f94f_c62442c8",
      "revId": "daa850c41f653c9e96ab9476bd999da913ce4260",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
